hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1269","Ali bin Al-Mundhir narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Abdul-Malik narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that he said: This verse was revealed: Wherever you turn, that is where God has directed. Surah Al-Baqarah, verse 115, that you should pray wherever your mount takes you in your journey. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace When he returns from Mecca, may God bless him and grant him peace, he voluntarily prays on his mount, nodding his head toward Medina."
